cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "DecoyFS: decoy-referenced feature selection"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-04"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/alexanderzrm/decoyfs"
keywords:
  - feature selection
  - decoy features
  - shadow features
  - random probes
  - tabular data
authors:
  - family-names: "Zermeño Campos"
    given-names: "Nestor A."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4638-4682"
    email: "nestor.zermeno@uabc.edu.mx"
    affiliation: "Universidad Autónoma de Baja California"
abstract: >-
  DecoyFS selects features by comparing real features against decoy (control) features, namely Random probes and
  Shadow copies, using several heterogeneous rankers and an auditable vote policy. Every component (rankers,
  controls, policy) is swappable; Boruta-style, CV-k and fixed-k comparators are included.
